1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,932
Trading bots want your keys, or a balance

2
00:00:02,962 --> 00:00:05,155
they can move however they like.

3
00:00:05,493 --> 00:00:08,215
XORR is for people who want an agent to

4
00:00:08,245 --> 00:00:11,082
trade crypto and perps for them, without

5
00:00:11,112 --> 00:00:12,652
handing it the money.

6
00:00:12,682 --> 00:00:15,972
A council of AI agents votes on every trade,

7
00:00:16,002 --> 00:00:19,200
inside a limit the chain enforces.

8
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:21,568
On Monad, a block is final in about half a

9
00:00:21,598 --> 00:00:24,354
second, so the vote and the fill happen

10
00:00:24,384 --> 00:00:25,380
together.

11
00:00:25,881 --> 00:00:27,790
One passkey makes the account.

12
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:30,658
No seed phrase, and nothing that can sign is

13
00:00:30,688 --> 00:00:31,774
stored.

14
00:00:31,804 --> 00:00:34,200
Test funds land, then the permission:

15
00:00:34,230 --> 00:00:37,498
a daily limit, an end date, the venues.

16
00:00:37,528 --> 00:00:39,855
It's signed without a wallet popup, and

17
00:00:39,885 --> 00:00:42,780
confirmed on chain ten seconds after the app

18
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:43,760
opened.

19
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:46,459
Buy twenty dollars of MON.

20
00:00:46,489 --> 00:00:48,839
Every order measures Kuru's on-chain order

21
00:00:48,869 --> 00:00:51,695
book against Uniswap v3, and fills on the

22
00:00:51,725 --> 00:00:55,318
better one. Here, Kuru beat Uniswap by a

23
00:00:55,348 --> 00:00:57,119
third of a percent.

24
00:00:57,149 --> 00:01:00,242
Two timers: executed in five hundred and ten

25
00:01:00,272 --> 00:01:02,611
milliseconds, with the receipt returned by

26
00:01:02,641 --> 00:01:03,934
the send itself.

27
00:01:03,964 --> 00:01:06,860
The gas cost a tenth of a cent, two hundred

28
00:01:06,890 --> 00:01:09,523
and twenty times less than on Ethereum.

29
00:01:10,023 --> 00:01:13,174
Now put fifty dollars of MON to the council.

30
00:01:13,204 --> 00:01:15,926
Price checks Chainlink against Kuru's book,

31
00:01:15,956 --> 00:01:18,735
Risk reads your limit, Trend and Perps read

32
00:01:18,765 --> 00:01:21,396
the market, and Kimi weighs them.

33
00:01:21,426 --> 00:01:24,357
Approved five to nothing, and filled:

34
00:01:24,387 --> 00:01:26,957
vote to fill in two tenths of a second.

35
00:01:26,987 --> 00:01:29,593
The replay shows what every seat read when

36
00:01:29,623 --> 00:01:30,782
it voted.

37
00:01:31,282 --> 00:01:35,130
Perps run on Perpl, with AUSD as margin,

38
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:37,846
through a desk that is Perpl's own delegated

39
00:01:37,876 --> 00:01:40,621
account. The agent can trade it.

40
00:01:40,651 --> 00:01:42,515
It can never withdraw.

41
00:01:42,545 --> 00:01:45,197
A long on MON, with its entry, mark and

42
00:01:45,227 --> 00:01:48,123
distance to liquidation, and standing exits

43
00:01:48,153 --> 00:01:50,503
checked every thirty seconds.

44
00:01:50,533 --> 00:01:53,045
Then it's closed, and the margin is back in

45
00:01:53,075 --> 00:01:54,176
the desk.

46
00:01:54,677 --> 00:01:57,468
Every grant, spend and desk is indexed by

47
00:01:57,498 --> 00:02:00,875
Envio's HyperIndex as the blocks arrive.

48
00:02:01,374 --> 00:02:04,386
Built on Monad reads the chain itself:

49
00:02:04,416 --> 00:02:07,625
commit states, the txpool, native staking,

50
00:02:07,655 --> 00:02:11,131
and Monad's P256 precompile, which checks

51
00:02:11,161 --> 00:02:14,027
this passkey's signature right here.

52
00:02:14,528 --> 00:02:16,878
And one hold stops everything.

53
00:02:16,908 --> 00:02:19,061
The permission is revoked and the desk's

54
00:02:19,091 --> 00:02:22,520
operator removed, on chain, and read back

55
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:23,884
from the chain.

56
00:02:24,383 --> 00:02:26,687
It's live on Monad testnet too.

57
00:02:26,717 --> 00:02:29,078
Here's a round from tonight, from a wallet

58
00:02:29,108 --> 00:02:30,738
we seeded and labelled:

59
00:02:30,768 --> 00:02:33,060
approved four to nothing, with Kimi's

60
00:02:33,090 --> 00:02:34,874
reasoning on screen.

61
00:02:34,904 --> 00:02:37,335
Each seat shows exactly what it read:

62
00:02:37,365 --> 00:02:39,820
Chainlink's price on Monad, the desk's

63
00:02:39,850 --> 00:02:42,124
limit, and Perpl's funding.

64
00:02:42,623 --> 00:02:44,729
And its fill, through the owner's Perpl

65
00:02:44,759 --> 00:02:47,195
desk, on Monad testnet.

66
00:02:47,696 --> 00:02:51,648
XORR. A council of AI agents trades for you

67
00:02:51,678 --> 00:02:55,523
on Monad, and one hold stops it on chain.

